<body><canvas id="matrix"></canvas><div class="page"><header class="wrap topbar"><a class="brand" href="index.html">MATRIX REPROGRAMMED</a><nav class="nav"><a href="membership.html">Membership</a><a href="billing-dashboard.html">Billing</a><a href="legal-notice.html">Legal Notice</a><a href="trust-privacy-policy.html">Privacy</a></nav></header><main class="wrap section"><div class="eyebrow">Version 2026-07-18-v1</div><h1>MEMBERSHIP TERMS.</h1><p class="lead">These terms govern Free Member accounts and optional recurring Supporter, Intelligence Member and Research Pro services.</p>
<section class="section"><h2>1. Membership levels</h2><p>Free Member access is €0 and never requires PayPal. Paid memberships are Supporter at €3 per month, Intelligence Member at €6 per month and Research Pro at €9 per month. The selected amount recurs monthly through PayPal until cancellation.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>2. What paid membership provides</h2><p>Paid levels add curation, delivery, monitoring, exports, research workflow tools, downloads and member services described on the membership page. The underlying public-source evidence remains available to Free Members. Membership does not guarantee a particular conclusion, the existence of a requested record, uninterrupted access to an external source, or completion of a priority request.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>3. Account and checkout</h2><p>A verified Matrix Reprogrammed account is required for paid checkout. PayPal approval alone does not grant paid access. The server grants or removes entitlements only from verified PayPal subscription and payment state. Checkout records the accepted terms version, recurring-payment acknowledgement, immediate-service request, withdrawal notice acknowledgement, member account, selected tier and timestamp.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>4. Billing and renewal</h2><p>Paid memberships renew monthly through PayPal at the price shown immediately before approval. PayPal may separately present its own terms, funding source and transaction details. A failed payment may trigger a limited grace state; repeated failure, suspension, refund, reversal or expiry can remove paid access in accordance with the verified billing state.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>5. Cancellation</h2><p>You may request cancellation from the Matrix Reprogrammed billing dashboard or through PayPal. Where PayPal confirms a paid period remains, access may continue until that period ends. Cancellation prevents future renewal; it does not automatically reverse a completed payment. The separate cancellation and withdrawal notice explains statutory rights and how to contact support.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>6. Immediate digital service and withdrawal rights</h2><p>Paid member services are digital services intended to begin after PayPal confirms an active subscription and the member expressly requests immediate performance. Statutory withdrawal rights remain available unless and only to the extent that an applicable legal exception has been validly triggered. Nothing in these terms removes mandatory consumer rights.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>7. Acceptable use</h2><p>Accounts and protected downloads are personal unless a separate licence says otherwise. Do not share login links, evade access controls, abuse research tools, submit unlawful material, target people without lawful purpose, or use the service to harass, threaten, impersonate or facilitate wrongdoing.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>8. Evidence and editorial boundary</h2><p>Matrix Reprogrammed distinguishes records, allegations, reporting, association, interpretation and speculation. A name appearing in a source or network does not itself prove guilt, knowledge or control. Corrections may be made when a source changes, a claim is overstated or an error is identified.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>9. Availability and changes</h2><p>Features may be improved, replaced or withdrawn where necessary for security, law, source availability or service integrity. A material adverse change to a paid service will be communicated through the member account or verified email route where reasonably possible. Current pricing and service descriptions are shown before checkout.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>10. Contact</h2><p>Membership and billing support: <a href="mailto:members@matrixreprogrammed.com">members@matrixreprogrammed.com</a>. Commercial operator details and the applicable consumer-mediation route must be completed and verified on the Legal Notice before live charging is enabled.</p></section>
